    <ns0:link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/huggingface/trl/releases/tag/v1.11.0" />
    <ns0:title>v1.11.0</ns0:title>
    <ns0:content type="html">&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Use vLLM's own server instead of TRL's&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;trl vllm-serve&lt;/code&gt; used to run a custom FastAPI app around vLLM's &lt;code&gt;LLM&lt;/code&gt;, with its own data-parallel fan-out and a worker extension for weight sync. vLLM's own server covers all of that. The custom server is gone: &lt;code&gt;trl/scripts/vllm_serve.py&lt;/code&gt; drops from &lt;strong&gt;1218 to ~130 lines&lt;/strong&gt; and now tran</ns0:content>
